-- **The confirmation step replaces the separate independent re-run (experiment; the mob's decision, card 178 retro).** While this entry is on trial, a Decider is recorded after its primary window and, when there was an amendment, the original protocol's confirmation step: each outlier's role is asked, with its own reply quoted, whether its adopted condition is met, and every other voter answers only whether the amendment changes their vote. The separate window of fresh seats on the final text (step 6, audit 13, finding F-038) is not run; it is run when any voter or the product owner asks for one, or when the primary window passed with no amendment and no seat voted No (so there is nothing to confirm) and the proposal is a change to this agreement. The record shows the primary window, each amendment and each confirmation, and carries one committed trigger line that an auditor can `git show`, naming which trigger applied: (a) the confirmation step completed, so the re-run was not run; (b) the re-run was run because a named voter or the product owner asked; (c) the re-run was run because the primary window passed with no No and no amendment and the proposal changes this agreement; (d) the re-run was not run because the primary window passed with no No and no amendment and the proposal does not change this agreement.
-  - Hypothesis: the confirmation step gives the check the re-run was meant to give (a result that does not rest on one noisy window) without fresh seats that never made the outlier's promise and raise new demands. Metric: minutes from proposal to recorded result per Decider (card 176: about 100 for three declaration Deciders; card 178: about 13 with one window and one confirmation step), target at most 20; Deciders that fail on a demand made only by a fresh re-run seat (D208, D209, D210, D212 and D214 had one), target 0. Counter-metric: single-window errors found after recording (a miscounted vote, a misread cite, a proposal adopted that a re-run would have failed). Trial: the next 5 Deciders. Decider D217, started 2026-11-08.
